        "method_name": "Score-weighte...",
        "tooltip": "Score-weighted combination of two strong single models for pairwise evidence selection. GPT-5.5 and Claude Fable 5 each independently choose which of two evidence images supports the claim, with Fable 5 additionally providing continuous per-image confidence scores. The two models' signals are summed (GPT-5.5's discrete choice contributes \u00b11, Fable 5 contributes its score difference), and the evidence item with the higher combined score is selected \u2014 so the two models agree on the large majority of items, and Fable 5's confidence arbitrates the small number of disagreements.",
